{
  "$comment": "Shared VfTextarea cases. Plain data only: no Vue, no PHP, no renderer objects. Each adapter maps these neutral fields onto its own API. The vocabulary is the historical Vue contract at fd793696f50d3be0fcd3788f0f8f751c63869963. Chosen for semantic coverage rather than a Cartesian grid, and deliberately much smaller than the VfInput catalog: this component has three props. \"props\" are declared component props, \"attrs\" fall through to the textarea, and \"field\" wraps the control in a real VfField. scripts/ci/textarea-coverage.mjs is what stops the list eroding.",
  "component": "textarea",
  "propVocabulary": {
    "modelValue": "The control value. Whitespace counts as filled: the test is string length, not content.",
    "size": "sm | md | lg. Defaults to md, which emits no size modifier.",
    "invalid": "Adds the invalid modifier and aria-invalid. A consumer aria-invalid overrides it."
  },
